.TH QUANUXCTL-EXT 1 "January 2026" "QuanuX" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quanuxctl-ext \- Manage QuanuX Extensions (QXP)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quanuxctl ext
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBext\fR command group manages the lifecycle of extensions. Extensions are sidecar processes that provide specialized capabilities (e.g., Broker connections, Indicators) to the QuanuX Core.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List all registered extensions found in the \fI/extensions\fR directory.
.RS
.B Output:
.br
- Name (e.g., "rithmic")
.br
- Status (Running/Stopped)
.br
- PID (if running)
.RE
.TP
.B run \fI<name>\fR
Run an extension in the \fBforeground\fR. This is the primary mode for development and debugging. Secrets are injected automatically.
.TP
.B start \fI<name>\fR
Start an extension as a \fBbackground daemon\fR. Logs are redirected to files.
.TP
.B stop \fI<name>\fR
Stop a running background extension.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B 1. Develop the Rithmic extension
.nf
$ quanuxctl ext run rithmic
.fi
.P
.B 2. Start Sierra Chart bridge in background
.nf
$ quanuxctl ext start sierra-chart
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quanuxctl (1),
.BR quanux-qxp (7)
